acklog is C$5.1B, which management says covers the C$4.2B guidance, and cancellations are under 1%. Backlog is not the same as 2027 revenue, though. It is likely spread over several years, and conversion depends on delivery capacity.\n- **The Q2 disruption:** A fire at the Halbrook plant stopped production for nine weeks in Q2 2026. Halbrook builds all of Voltaris's large power transformers. The plant restarted in August at full capacity, and the delayed orders are to be delivered under a delivery recovery plan. This looks like a timing hit, not a loss of demand. Q2 revenue was C$890M, against C$980M in Q1.\n- **Run rate:** The last four quarters were C$905M, C$960M, C$980M and C$890M. Normal-quarter revenue is about C$950–980M, which annualises to roughly C$3.8–3.9B. Reaching C$4.2B needs about 8–10% growth over that run rate. Orders up 11% and the recovery deliveries make that plausible, but it leaves little margin.\n- **Recovery plan:** I did not find the plan's details, such as the amounts or the timing of the recovery deliveries. I'm assuming the lost Q2 revenue (roughly C$70–90M) is recovered in H2 2026 or 2027.\n\n**Risks:**\n- The recovery plan could slip.\n- Backlog may convert more slowly than management implies.\n- Industry transformer shipments fell 4% year on year in Q2 2026. That is the angle n3 is covering, and its preliminary view is below guidance.","ttft_ms":1965,"type":"result","duration_ms":46128,"uuid":"57edecbe-878f-4d8a-bcf1-f07473b17aa8","ttft_stream_ms":1139,"time_to_request_ms":197,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":15,"system_prompt":11,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":32,"input_hooks":7,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":22,"tool_pool_refresh":8,"init_message":14,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":10,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":32,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":4,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":9,"requ